    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d432">

                <pb facs="0599" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg507"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/9499a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-09T13:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 9, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7201. Department would appreciate a cable from you setting out following details
                    concerning Allied Maritime Transport Council: (1) Names of representatives of
                    Great Britain, France and Italy on this council. (2) Statement of its functions
                    and the character of the questions it considers.</p>
                <p>This information undoubtedly can be obtained by you after consultation with
                        Stevens and with other members of
                    Council.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
